/P 201 0 R
/T (Each year, more than 700 youth age out of foster care in Texas. Between 2020 and 2025, this number ranged from 740 to 1,256, for a total of 5,888 youth.3 Based on national trends, up to 46% of these youth will experience homelessness by the age of 26, with approximately 12% of youth transitioning out of care and directly into homelessness.4   )
/E (Each year, more than 700 youth age out of foster care in Texas. Between 2020 and 2025, this number ranged from 740 to 1,256, for a total of 5,888 youth.3 Based on national trends, up to 46% of these youth will experience homelessness by the age of 26, with approximately 12% of youth transitioning out of care and directly into homelessness.4   )
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [7 10 8 11 9 12]
>>
endobj
213 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 201 0 R
/T (Currently, there are 641 FYI vouchers allocated to Texas, but only 75% are currently in use. Accounting for the vouchers that are already utilized, an estimated 1,859 aged-out youth in Texas are eligible for an FYI voucher. Ensuring that aged-out youth experiencing homelessness or housing instability have access to supportive services until their 25th birthday would allow all eligible youth to access available FYI vouchers.)
/E (Currently, there are 641 FYI vouchers allocated to Texas, but only 75% are currently in use. Accounting for the vouchers that are already utilized, an estimated 1,859 aged-out youth in Texas are eligible for an FYI voucher. Ensuring that aged-out youth experiencing homelessness or housing instability have access to supportive services until their 25th birthday would allow all eligible youth to access available FYI vouchers.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [13 15 14]
>>
