/Title (Each year, more than 700 youth age out of foster care in Texas. Between 2020 and 2025, this number ranged from 740 to 1,256, for a total of 5,888 youth.3 Based on national trends, up to 46% of these youth will experience homelessness by the age of 26, with approximately 12% of youth transitioning out of care and directly into homelessness.4)
