/Title (Youth aging out of foster care are at a greater risk of experiencing homelessness and housing instability in early adulthood which, in turn, increases the risk of adult chronic homelessness. The year-over-year cost of inaction is substantial, with annual per-capita spending for each unhoused individual totaling $43,901.5 That is roughly $30,000 more per person than the $10,500 needed to ensure foster youth receive housing and supportive services to avoid homelessness.)
